<%- include('_partials/head', { pageStyles: ['/css/kurukoo-channel-page.css'] }) %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>
<% const statuses = typeof channelStatuses === 'object' && channelStatuses ? channelStatuses : {}; const aiState = process.env.KURUKOO_MCP_ENABLED === 'true' ? 'READY' : 'NOT_CONFIGURED'; const aiNote = process.env.KURUKOO_MCP_ENABLED === 'true' ? 'One remote MCP connection surface for compatible AI assistants. Availability of write actions depends on the external assistant.' : 'Enable KURUKOO_MCP_ENABLED and configure the public HTTPS issuer/client relationship before allowing external AI control.'; const label = (key, fallback) => String(statuses[key]?.state || fallback || 'NOT_CONFIGURED').replaceAll('_', ' '); %>
<main class="container page-container">
  <section class="page-header-center"><span class="badge-pill">Channels & connections</span><h1 class="page-title">Connect Kurukoo to the channels and AI assistants you already use.</h1><p class="page-desc">Every connection enters the same Kurukoo relationship. Provider delivery, identity, canonical state and external evidence are shown truthfully instead of presenting an inactive integration as connected.</p></section>
  <section class="channel-group"><h2 class="channel-group-title">AI assistants</h2><div class="channel-cards">
    <article id="ai-assistants" class="channel-card <%= aiState === 'READY' ? 'available' : 'unavailable' %>"><div class="channel-icon">AI</div><span class="channel-state <%= aiState === 'READY' ? 'active' : '' %>"><%= aiState.replaceAll('_', ' ') %></span><h3>AI assistants</h3><p><%= aiNote %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>One Kurukoo MCP endpoint</strong> Compatible clients may include ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, Copilot, Dola and other assistants that support remote MCP/custom apps. Connect through OAuth; Kurukoo never receives another AI provider's password, session or subscription credential.</div><a href="/connect#ai-assistants" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">View connection settings</a></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="channel-group"><h2 class="channel-group-title">Your access points</h2><div class="channel-cards"><article class="channel-card available"><div class="channel-icon">W</div><span class="channel-state active">READY</span><h3>Web Chat</h3><p>Start a conversation, review request details, manage reminders and continue protected actions when identity is required.</p><a href="/chat" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">Start chatting</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="channel-group"><h2 class="channel-group-title">Set up a channel</h2><p class="channel-note">These adapters are repository-complete and remain inactive only when deployment credentials, provider contracts or runtime infrastructure are absent. Configure the documented keys, restart the service, then verify provider delivery.</p><div class="channel-cards">
    <article id="whatsapp" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">WA</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('whatsapp') %></span><h3>WhatsApp</h3><p><%= statuses.whatsapp?.note || 'The official WhatsApp adapter uses the canonical Chat identity and webhook boundary.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Set <code>WHATSAPP_TOKEN</code>, <code>WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID</code>, webhook verification values and the provider callback. Signature verification, inbound normalization, canonical Chat routing and outbound formatting are already wired.</div></article>
    <article id="telegram" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">TG</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('telegram') %></span><h3>Telegram</h3><p><%= statuses.telegram?.note || 'Telegram uses the shared channel and conversation authority.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Set <code>TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN</code> and <code>TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>, register the callback, and verify delivery.</div></article>
    <article id="sms" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">SMS</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('sms') %></span><h3>SMS</h3><p><%= statuses.sms?.note || 'SMS uses normalized phone identity and the canonical request lifecycle.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Set the carrier adapter credentials such as <code>AFRICASTALKING_API_KEY</code> and <code>AFRICASTALKING_USERNAME</code>, then verify inbound and outbound delivery.</div></article>
    <article id="ussd" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">US</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('ussd') %></span><h3>USSD</h3><p><%= statuses.ussd?.note || 'USSD menus map feature-phone input into the same identity and request semantics.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Set carrier routing and callback credentials. Menu state, pagination, session handling and short prompts remain provider-independent.</div></article>
    <article id="email" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">EM</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('email') %></span><h3>Email</h3><p><%= statuses.email?.note || 'Email inbound and outbound paths preserve the canonical conversation boundary.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Set <code>RESEND_API_KEY</code>, <code>EMAIL_FROM</code> and signed webhook configuration, then verify message and delivery callbacks.</div></article>
    <article id="fcm" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">FC</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('fcm') %></span><h3>Push notifications</h3><p><%= statuses.fcm?.note || 'Internal notifications remain available when external push is not configured.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Provide FCM credentials and verify provider delivery. Internal inbox persistence does not become a false external “sent” claim.</div></article>
    <article id="voice" class="channel-card unavailable"><div class="channel-icon">VO</div><span class="channel-state"><%= label('voice') %></span><h3>Web Voice</h3><p><%= statuses.voice?.note || 'Voice remains the same Kurukoo relationship with bounded realtime tools.' %></p><div class="channel-setup"><strong>Activation boundary</strong>Enable <code>KURUKOO_VOICE_ENABLED=true</code> with the configured realtime provider credential and verify applicable quota.</div></article>
  </div></section>
</main>
<%- include('_partials/footer') %>